WEBVTT

00:08:29.970 --> 00:08:31.599
paid the rent and stuff like that.

00:08:31.623 --> 00:08:33.020
And I needed a check.

00:08:33.044 --> 00:08:34.654
AG: It went well, at first.

00:08:35.036 --> 00:08:38.409
But then the interviewer asked her
to do some math on the spot,

00:08:38.433 --> 00:08:40.850
specifically, long division.

00:08:40.874 --> 00:08:44.248
LR: And I completely blanked.

00:08:44.272 --> 00:08:46.353
I couldn't remember which number,

00:08:46.377 --> 00:08:48.808
which was the numerator,
which was the denominator,

00:08:48.832 --> 00:08:49.991
what you divided,

00:08:50.015 --> 00:08:52.601
which number on which side
of the little long division,

00:08:52.625 --> 00:08:53.828
little monkey bars things

00:08:53.852 --> 00:08:56.155
you're supposed to actually
put within the other,

00:08:56.179 --> 00:08:57.333
and I froze.

00:08:57.357 --> 00:08:59.456
And the interviewer
turned to me and he said,

00:08:59.480 --> 00:09:01.817
"I cannot believe you got into Yale."